# Verify Newly Written Code

After writing or materially changing Rust, build, or packaging files, run from the workspace root, in order:

1. `make fmt` — apply rustfmt
2. `make check` — `check-fmt` + clippy (`-D warnings`, default features) + `cargo deny` (Linux graph)
3. `make test` — nextest workspace + Linux `sqyre-capture --features portal-capture` pass; crate-only `cargo test -p …` does not count

All must exit 0 before saying the work is done or opening a PR. On failure, fix the cause and re-run from `make fmt`. Do not silence Clippy with broad `#[allow]` or weaken workspace lint policy.

Also run when relevant (CI enforces the first three):
- Dependencies changed → `make machete`
- Code in a crate listed in `scripts/coverage-floors.json` → `make coverage-floors`
- `sqyre-app` UI or crates it uses → `make wasm-check` (see `wasm-editor`)
- `portal-capture` / Wayland code → `cargo clippy -p sqyre-capture --features portal-capture --all-targets -- -D warnings`
- Windows-only code (`win_*`, `#[cfg(windows)]`) → `make windows`, or state it was not compiled

The final summary names which gates ran and their result, plus any blocker.

Skip only for docs/markdown/rule-only edits, read-only investigation, or when the user explicitly waives it. Prefer these targets over ad-hoc cargo so flags match CI.
